---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PolicyContact from "../components/PolicyContact.astro";
import { LEGAL_HOLDER, SITE_URL, SOURCE_URL } from "../data/site";
---

<Layout
  title="The Bead Reserve : Terms"
  description="The terms for using The Bead Reserve's website, covering the status of the token and the license for the code."
>
  <main>
    <article class="policy bracket-frame">
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Last updated: October 8, 2026</p>
        <p>
          The Bead Reserve
          (<a href={`${SITE_URL}/`}>beadz.half-built-robots.com</a>) is owned
          and operated by {LEGAL_HOLDER}, a California LLC. By using the site
          you agree to these terms.
        </p>

        <h2 id="using-the-site">Using the site</h2>
        <p>
          You may read, link to, and share the site's content for your own
          personal, noncommercial purposes. The site's words, the whitepaper's
          text, the artwork (including Henry, the robot mascot, and the reserve
          seal), and the site design are copyright {LEGAL_HOLDER}, all rights
          reserved. Quoting a short passage with attribution and a link back is
          fine. Otherwise, do not republish or redistribute content from this
          site, or present it as your own work, without written permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Third-party names, including Base, Ethereum, and the wallet brands,
          belong to their owners.
        </p>
        <p>
          Search engines and AI crawlers are welcome to index the site, and AI
          developers are welcome to train on it.
        </p>

        <h2>The token</h2>
        <p>
          BEADZ is a novelty collectible issued for amusement. It has no
          monetary value, and none is promised. It carries no expectation of
          profit. It is not a stablecoin, a security, a deposit, or a payment
          instrument, and it is not pegged to any national currency. I sell it
          to no one and seed no market. Any market a third party creates is that
          party's doing and risk.
        </p>
        <p>
          Physical redemption is available by prepaid certified mail with
          signature, in minimum lots, while the redemption window is open. It
          costs far more than the beads are worth. The
          <a href="/whitepaper.pdf">whitepaper</a> sets out the full terms.
        </p>
        <p>Nothing on this site is financial or legal advice.</p>

        <h2>On-chain transactions</h2>
        <p>
          Claims and redemptions are transactions on Base that you sign with
          your own wallet. Transactions on Base are public and permanent. Once
          one is confirmed, it cannot be reversed. I cannot recover a lost key
          or undo a transaction, and I cannot return tokens sent to the wrong
          address.
        </p>
        <p>
          You pay the network fee for each transaction, in ETH. A redemption
          burns your tokens at the moment of the transaction.
        </p>

        <h2>Code</h2>
        <p>
          The software behind The Bead Reserve (the contract, the camera, the
          service, and this site's code) is published under the
          <a href={`${SOURCE_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT license</a> in the
          <a href={SOURCE_URL}>public repository</a>. Anything the license
          allows is allowed here, provided the copyright and license notice
          travel with the code.
        </p>
        <p>
          The site's words and the whitepaper's text are not covered by that
          grant. They are reserved under
          <a href="#using-the-site">Using the site</a> above.
        </p>

        <h2>Brand assets</h2>
        <p>
          Henry and the reserve seal are excluded from the MIT grant under the
          BRAND ASSETS EXCEPTION in the repository's <code>LICENSE</code>. They
          are &copy; {LEGAL_HOLDER}, all rights reserved. You may use them to
          refer to The Bead Reserve. Neither they nor the name "The Bead
          Reserve" may be used as the identity of another project, a fork of
          this one included. The <a href="/brand/">brand assets</a> page sets
          out the usage rules.
        </p>

        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site and the token are provided "as is" and "as available",
          without warranties of any kind, express or implied. The reserve is
          uninsured. To the maximum extent permitted by law, {LEGAL_HOLDER} is
          not liable for any damages arising from your use of, or inability to
          use, the site or the token, or from reliance on the site's content.
        </p>

        <h2>Indemnity</h2>
        <p>
          If you fork the software or deploy your own vault, you do so at your
          own risk. You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {LEGAL_HOLDER}
          against claims arising from that use, to the extent the law allows.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          The site sets no cookies of its own. Cloudflare, the site's host, sets
          one security cookie, and the site keeps two small values in your
          browser's local storage. The
          <a href="/privacy/#cookies-and-browser-storage">privacy policy</a>
          lists each one and what it's for.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          The site links to the Half-Built Robots blog and to other sites. Those
          sites are not under my control and a link is not an endorsement. Their
          terms and privacy practices are their own.
        </p>

        <h2>Copyright complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you believe content on this site infringes your copyright, contact
          me using the information below and I will review and address it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms may change. Updates are posted on this page with a new
          date at the top. Continued use of the site after a change means you
          accept the updated terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California,
          United States, without regard to its conflict of law provisions.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <PolicyContact />
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
